                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For a horizontal dilation by a factor of $h$, replace $x\\mapsto \\frac{x}{h}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=a^{x/h}\\\\\\ln y&=\\frac{x}{h}\\ln a\\end{align*}$$\nFor the target $y=b^x$, $\\ln y=x\\ln b$. Comparing the coefficients of $x$ gives\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\ln a}{h}&=\\ln b\\\\h&=\\frac{\\ln a}{\\ln b}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $a,b>1$, both logarithms are positive, so this is a valid positive dilation factor.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 70
