                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "For a vertical dilation by a factor of $k$, replace $y\\mapsto \\frac{y}{k}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{k}&=a^x\\\\y&=ka^x\\end{align*}$$\nTo equal $y=b^x$, at $x=0$ we need\n$$\\begin{align*}k&=1\\end{align*}$$\nThen at $x=1$ we need $a=b$, contrary to the given $a\\ne b$. Therefore no vertical dilation gives the required graph.",
